IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cf66-nouns`
IMPORT `cf66-cross-references`

-- Row il-66. The controls hold, and the recorded facts about the four items are what NOTES.md says they are.
-- The defects themselves are NOT asserted sound anywhere in this file: the six failing assertions are in cf66-tests-xrefs-red.l4. Where a record is shown to differ from a sound reading, the negation of the failing assertion is stated here and passes.
-- Every expected value is written from the texts quoted in cf66-cross-references.l4, not from the output of the module.

§ `Tests of the sound controls`

-- I1 control: the saving clause of the amending regulations says that the earlier regulations continue for proceedings opened before the commencement day, qualified by a rule of the new regulations.
#ASSERT (`saving clause: section 3 of the amending regulations, KT 8085 p. 470`)'s `the earlier regulations continue for proceedings opened before the commencement day`
#ASSERT (`saving clause: section 3 of the amending regulations, KT 8085 p. 470`)'s `the continuation is qualified by a rule of the new regulations on which proceedings they apply to`
-- I1 control for the arithmetic: the comparison tells apart a range that holds the number from a range that does not (it is not the case that every number is inside every range).
#ASSERT `the rule cited lies inside the range` (`cited rule: 143 in the definition of the pre-trial session`) (`range: regulations 132 to 258 cancelled, KT 8085 p. 470`)
#ASSERT NOT `the rule cited lies inside the range` (`cited rule: 143 in the definition of the pre-trial session`) (`range: regulations 1 to 131(ב) cancelled, KT 8085 p. 470`)
#ASSERT NOT `the rule cited lies inside the range` (`cited rule: 143 in the definition of the pre-trial session`) (`range: regulations 360 to 532 cancelled, KT 8085 p. 470`)
#ASSERT NOT `the rule cited lies inside the range` (`cited rule: 214 with a letter after it, in the same definition`) (`range: regulations 1 to 131(ב) cancelled, KT 8085 p. 470`)
#ASSERT NOT `the rule cited lies inside the range` (`cited rule: 214 with a letter after it, in the same definition`) (`range: regulations 360 to 532 cancelled, KT 8085 p. 470`)
-- I2 control: the 2018 citation gives no subsection and the section it cites is printed by the consolidation.
#ASSERT `the citation resolves to what the consolidation prints` (`power citation: KT 7980 cites 83, no subsection`)
#ASSERT NOT (`power citation: KT 7980 cites 83, no subsection`)'s `the citing words give a subsection`
-- I3 control: the rates that the two items print agree.
#ASSERT (`threshold: item 8 of the 2013 notice, KT 7199 p. 400`)'s `the first rate printed, in percent` EQUALS (`threshold: item 22 of the 2013 notice, KT 7199 p. 401`)'s `the first rate printed, in percent`
#ASSERT (`threshold: item 8 of the 2013 notice, KT 7199 p. 400`)'s `the second rate printed, in percent` EQUALS (`threshold: item 22 of the 2013 notice, KT 7199 p. 401`)'s `the second rate printed, in percent`
-- I4 control: the notice was signed before the suspension was signed.
#ASSERT `the notice was signed before the suspension was signed` (`item 36 as the 2021 notice prints it, KT 9099 p. 1565`) (`suspension: KT 9089 p. 1524`)

§ `Tests of what the records say (I1)`

-- The two numbers cited and the letter on the second; the second is compared by its base number.
#ASSERT (`cited rule: 143 in the definition of the pre-trial session`)'s `the rule as the citing words print it` EQUALS "143"
#ASSERT (`cited rule: 143 in the definition of the pre-trial session`)'s `the base number of the rule` EQUALS 143
#ASSERT (`cited rule: 214 with a letter after it, in the same definition`)'s `the rule as the citing words print it` EQUALS "214יא"
#ASSERT (`cited rule: 214 with a letter after it, in the same definition`)'s `the base number of the rule` EQUALS 214
-- The three ranges as the cancelling words print them.
#ASSERT count (`the ranges that regulation 2 cancels`) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT (`range: regulations 132 to 258 cancelled, KT 8085 p. 470`)'s `the first number of the range` EQUALS 132
#ASSERT (`range: regulations 132 to 258 cancelled, KT 8085 p. 470`)'s `the last number of the range` EQUALS 258
#ASSERT (`range: regulations 1 to 131(ב) cancelled, KT 8085 p. 470`)'s `the last number of the range` EQUALS 131
#ASSERT (`range: regulations 360 to 532 cancelled, KT 8085 p. 470`)'s `the first number of the range` EQUALS 360
-- Each cited number lies inside exactly one of the ranges (the negation of the failing assertions of cf66-tests-xrefs-red.l4).
#ASSERT `how many of the ranges hold the rule cited` (`cited rule: 143 in the definition of the pre-trial session`) (`the ranges that regulation 2 cancels`) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `how many of the ranges hold the rule cited` (`cited rule: 214 with a letter after it, in the same definition`) (`the ranges that regulation 2 cancels`) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the rule cited lies inside one of the ranges` (`cited rule: 143 in the definition of the pre-trial session`) (`the ranges that regulation 2 cancels`)
#ASSERT `the rule cited lies inside one of the ranges` (`cited rule: 214 with a letter after it, in the same definition`) (`the ranges that regulation 2 cancels`)
#ASSERT NOT `the rule cited lies outside every one of the ranges` (`cited rule: 143 in the definition of the pre-trial session`) (`the ranges that regulation 2 cancels`)
#ASSERT NOT `the rule cited lies outside every one of the ranges` (`cited rule: 214 with a letter after it, in the same definition`) (`the ranges that regulation 2 cancels`)
-- Where each reading comes from: the citing words and the cancelling ranges from the official pages, crops deposited; the saving clause likewise.
#ASSERT (`cited rule: 143 in the definition of the pre-trial session`)'s `the citing words were read from` EQUALS `the official page, read from its image, and the cropped image is deposited`
#ASSERT (`range: regulations 132 to 258 cancelled, KT 8085 p. 470`)'s `the range was read from` EQUALS `the official page, read from its image, and the cropped image is deposited`
#ASSERT (`saving clause: section 3 of the amending regulations, KT 8085 p. 470`)'s `the saving clause was read from` EQUALS `the official page, read from its image, and the cropped image is deposited`
-- The commencement day of the new regulations, as two labelled readings; the row states no commencement day of its own. Each printed Gregorian date is the day the Hebrew-calendar routine gives for the printed Hebrew date.
#ASSERT (`commencement: as made, from the page`)'s `the Gregorian date printed` EQUALS (`commencement: as made, from the page`)'s `the day the Hebrew date falls on, by the routine`
#ASSERT (`commencement: as the consolidation prints it today`)'s `the Gregorian date printed` EQUALS (`commencement: as the consolidation prints it today`)'s `the day the Hebrew date falls on, by the routine`
#ASSERT (`commencement: as made, from the page`)'s `the Gregorian date printed` EQUALS Date 5 9 2019
#ASSERT (`commencement: as the consolidation prints it today`)'s `the Gregorian date printed` EQUALS Date 1 1 2021
#ASSERT NOT ((`commencement: as made, from the page`)'s `the Gregorian date printed` EQUALS (`commencement: as the consolidation prints it today`)'s `the Gregorian date printed`)
#ASSERT (`commencement: as made, from the page`)'s `the reading was read from` EQUALS `the official page, read from its image, and the cropped image is deposited`
#ASSERT (`commencement: as the consolidation prints it today`)'s `the reading was read from` EQUALS `the consolidation only`
-- Rule 143 of the new regulations, as the page prints it.
#ASSERT (`rule as the new regulations print it: 143 on KT 8085 p. 452`)'s `the number of the rule as printed` EQUALS 143
#ASSERT (`rule as the new regulations print it: 143 on KT 8085 p. 452`)'s `the margin note, in English` EQUALS "joining of appeals"

§ `Tests of what the records say (I2)`

-- The citation of 2021 gives the section 83 and the subsection as "3"; the consolidation prints the labels (א) and (ב) under s 83.
#ASSERT (`power citation: KT 9735 cites 83(3)`)'s `the section cited` EQUALS 83
#ASSERT (`power citation: KT 9735 cites 83(3)`)'s `the citing words give a subsection`
#ASSERT (`power citation: KT 9735 cites 83(3)`)'s `the subsection cited, as written` EQUALS "3"
#ASSERT (`power citation: KT 9735 cites 83(3)`)'s `the section is printed by the consolidation`
#ASSERT count ((`power citation: KT 9735 cites 83(3)`)'s `the subsection labels the consolidation prints in the section`) EQUALS 2
-- The consolidation prints no subsection under the label "3" (0 of 1), and so the citation does not resolve by that label (the negation of the failing assertions).
#ASSERT `how many subsections the consolidation prints under the label the citing words give` (`power citation: KT 9735 cites 83(3)`) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT NOT `the consolidation prints a subsection under the label the citing words give` (`power citation: KT 9735 cites 83(3)`)
#ASSERT NOT `the citation resolves to what the consolidation prints` (`power citation: KT 9735 cites 83(3)`)
-- Where each side was read from: the citing words from the official page, the crop deposited; the target from the consolidation only.
#ASSERT (`power citation: KT 9735 cites 83(3)`)'s `the opening words were read from` EQUALS `the official page, read from its image, and the cropped image is deposited`
#ASSERT (`power citation: KT 9735 cites 83(3)`)'s `the target was read from` EQUALS `the consolidation only`
#ASSERT (`power citation: KT 7980 cites 83, no subsection`)'s `the section cited` EQUALS 83

§ `Tests of what the records say (I3)`

-- The two figures printed beside the word that opens the threshold, their difference, and that the records do not agree (the negation of the failing assertion).
#ASSERT (`threshold: item 8 of the 2013 notice, KT 7199 p. 400`)'s `the figure printed beside the word that opens the threshold` EQUALS 23800859
#ASSERT (`threshold: item 22 of the 2013 notice, KT 7199 p. 401`)'s `the figure printed beside the word that opens the threshold` EQUALS 23880859
#ASSERT `the difference between the two figures` (`threshold: item 8 of the 2013 notice, KT 7199 p. 400`) (`threshold: item 22 of the 2013 notice, KT 7199 p. 401`) EQUALS 80000
#ASSERT NOT `the two items print the same figure` (`threshold: item 8 of the 2013 notice, KT 7199 p. 400`) (`threshold: item 22 of the 2013 notice, KT 7199 p. 401`)
-- A figure agrees with itself (the comparison can say yes).
#ASSERT `the two items print the same figure` (`threshold: item 8 of the 2013 notice, KT 7199 p. 400`) (`threshold: item 8 of the 2013 notice, KT 7199 p. 400`)
-- Both items were read from the official pages, the crops deposited.
#ASSERT (`threshold: item 8 of the 2013 notice, KT 7199 p. 400`)'s `the threshold was read from` EQUALS `the official page, read from its image, and the cropped image is deposited`
#ASSERT (`threshold: item 22 of the 2013 notice, KT 7199 p. 401`)'s `the threshold was read from` EQUALS `the official page, read from its image, and the cropped image is deposited`

§ `Tests of what the records say (I4)`

-- The dates the pages print, in order: the notice signed, the suspension signed, the suspension published, the notice published; the end of the window.
#ASSERT (`item 36 as the 2021 notice prints it, KT 9099 p. 1565`)'s `the notice was signed on` EQUALS Date 21 12 2020
#ASSERT (`suspension: KT 9089 p. 1524`)'s `the suspension was signed on` EQUALS Date 11 1 2021
#ASSERT (`suspension: KT 9089 p. 1524`)'s `the suspension was published on` EQUALS Date 12 1 2021
#ASSERT (`item 36 as the 2021 notice prints it, KT 9099 p. 1565`)'s `the notice was published on` EQUALS Date 17 1 2021
#ASSERT (`suspension: KT 9089 p. 1524`)'s `the last day of the period` EQUALS Date 20 7 2021
#ASSERT (`suspension: KT 9089 p. 1524`)'s `the suspension was signed on` AT MOST (`suspension: KT 9089 p. 1524`)'s `the suspension was published on`
#ASSERT (`suspension: KT 9089 p. 1524`)'s `the suspension was published on` AT MOST (`item 36 as the 2021 notice prints it, KT 9099 p. 1565`)'s `the notice was published on`
-- The amount printed beside item 36, and the flag that it is the item that regulation 4(3) of the 2017 temporary regulations adds.
#ASSERT (`item 36 as the 2021 notice prints it, KT 9099 p. 1565`)'s `the item number` EQUALS 36
#ASSERT (`item 36 as the 2021 notice prints it, KT 9099 p. 1565`)'s `the amount printed beside the item` EQUALS 36
#ASSERT (`item 36 as the 2021 notice prints it, KT 9099 p. 1565`)'s `the item is the item that regulation 4(3) of the 2017 temporary regulations adds`
-- The suspension treats regulation 1 and paragraph (3) of regulation 4 of the 2017 temporary regulations as cancelled for the period.
#ASSERT (`suspension: KT 9089 p. 1524`)'s `regulation 1 of the 2017 temporary regulations is treated as cancelled`
#ASSERT (`suspension: KT 9089 p. 1524`)'s `paragraph (3) of regulation 4 of the 2017 temporary regulations is treated as cancelled`
-- The publication day of the notice falls inside the period, and so the notice's item is treated as cancelled on that day (the negation of the failing assertion).
#ASSERT `the item is treated as cancelled on the day the notice was published` (`item 36 as the 2021 notice prints it, KT 9099 p. 1565`) (`suspension: KT 9089 p. 1524`)
#ASSERT NOT `the notice prints no amount for an item treated as cancelled on its publication day` (`item 36 as the 2021 notice prints it, KT 9099 p. 1565`) (`suspension: KT 9089 p. 1524`)
-- Where each reading comes from: all from the official pages, the crops deposited.
#ASSERT (`item 36 as the 2021 notice prints it, KT 9099 p. 1565`)'s `the item row was read from` EQUALS `the official page, read from its image, and the cropped image is deposited`
#ASSERT (`suspension: KT 9089 p. 1524`)'s `the suspension was read from` EQUALS `the official page, read from its image, and the cropped image is deposited`
